ACID2000 v.2

ACID2000 is an advanced caller ID detector,
voice manager and telephone answering machine
for voice modems.
ACID2000 resides in your System Tray, where it
monitors and handles your incoming voice calls.
You can set up ACID2000 to automatically accept
or reject an incoming call by adding any caller's
ID to your "Black List", thus ensuring that their
calls do not ring through. 

ACID2000 also performs the functions of a standard
telephone answering machine. In this mode it can 
play your greeting, send a beep signal and record
message, and hang up when the call is complete. 

Incoming call actions can be set to not answer,
answer immediately or after a specified number
of rings, record the message or start the answering
machine sequence, or set your caller on hold and
play music to the line. Once you accept a call you
then have the option of recording part or all of 
your conversation to a standard WAV file for your
records.
